WEBVTT

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.880
I ain't good at these things.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.520
Well, I'm Soshigaya Guren.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.710
That's my real name.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.060
I'm an orphan.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.810
The moment I was kicked 
out of the orphanage,

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.350
I got picked up by old man, Hatonami,

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.460
and I decided to follow 
him the rest of my life.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:36.730
For him, I'm ready to die at any time.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.760
He fights with a Japanese sword, right?

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:48.440
So, I honed my skills with a gun, 
so I can back him up.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:53.470
A gun tends to work fairly 
well against Gibia, too.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.650
But I've got no bullets.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:03.130
I bet getting rid of all its guns

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.730
is why Japan was overrun 
by Gibia so quickly.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:16.270
Huh? Other countries 
are just as overrun with Gibia?

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.200
Whole world's really coming to end, huh?

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.440
<b>"Until It All Burns Out"</b>

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.300
What's wrong?

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.600
That's...!

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.650
What happened?!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.240
Old...

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.770
Old man!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.740
Hey! Hang in there!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.320
Yukinojyo!

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.800
Monk!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.790
What happened here?!

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.310
Yukinojyo-san!

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.710
Yukinojyo-san!

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.820
Open your eyes!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.520
The fact he hasn't turned into a Gibia

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:34.580
means he was stabbed repeatedly 
by ones without their poison, right?

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.400
I'm sorry.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.300
If I had given you a proper 
charm instead of one for studies,

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.600
maybe you wouldn't have died...

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.590
Yukinojyo-san...

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.910
Th-Those clothes...

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:22.610
<i>Yurika-san... came back as a Gibia, then.</i>

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:28.190
<i>The monk couldn't have fought 
at full strength against that.</i>

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:05.310
It's an awful world 
when the good people die first.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.120
Kenroku, what happened?

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.110
Well...

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.670
Yukinojyo.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.530
Thank you for protecting Kathleen.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.750
I'm sorry I couldn't get up.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.900
From today on, you'll live with me.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.070
As my eternal friend.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.710
<i>Right.</i>

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:01.860
<i>This is how Sensui must have 
bid farewell to his friends, too.</i>

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.050
Hey, I heard a weird sound.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.420
We okay?

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:14.780
Wh-What?

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.470
We've got no luck!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.500
We've got bad luck.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:31.610
No, looks like it ain't that bad.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:33.920
Huh?

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.780
Lucky us!

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.120
We should be able to repair the van now!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:54.270
Well, there are probably Gibia around.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.510
I'm back with some food.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.410
Hey, good work.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:18.620
W-We picked up a whole lot.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:22.220
Oh, how considerate.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.960
But these...

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.300
need hot water.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:35.780
Jeez. This is your fault for saying 
you wanted to eat some cup noodles.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.780
B-B-But I do want to eat something hot.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:44.960
Looks like the Gibia are going to come out 
before we can find a kettle.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.620
Th-Th-Th-Th-There they are!

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:01.830
What?! What's going on?

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.660
That, that, that, that!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.830
Hey, what happened to your explosives?!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.330
I forgot to bring them!

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.020
Without your bombs, you're just a fatass!

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.540
Damn it! Why, you...! You...!

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.010
Y-You two are incredible!

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.610
Th-There are more!

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.130
The exit!

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:03.830
Hey, are you okay?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.250
W-We're safe.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.450
What now?

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.160
If we leave them alone, 
they'll come out at night and attack us.

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:19.110
We should beat it on out of here.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.640
The van's still not fixed yet.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:26.050
Well, what to do...

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.100
Let's go!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.500
Yeah!

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:44.060
Here they fucking come.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.300
Fall back!

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.870
Wh-Where's Mikimoto?

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:06.200
Mikimoto! Jump!

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.500
Hamuro! Now!

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:24.430
We did it!

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:25.960
Yeah!

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.590
I-I'm hungry now.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:33.220
Go eat some Gibia.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.010
They're fried up nice.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.400
N-No way!

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:49.820
Wouldn't eating Gibia turn you into one?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.150
Our boss isn't feeling too good.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.110
Can't blame him.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.960
Not after everything 
his daughter said to him.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.020
Hey.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:35.760
Stealing from the living 
might be a yakuza's job,

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:40.130
but disrespecting the dead 
is straying from the path.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:53.800
Still, an enemy is an enemy, regardless.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.470
Hey, you guys, we're leaving.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.620
From what's here on the map,

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:16.270
the Gibia Virus Treatment Research Center 
should be just a little further up ahead.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.290
Meaning?

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.080
We might be able to 
find some research data there

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.890
that would help us develop a vaccine.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:28.790
It will be a detour, but it's worth the trip.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:32.670
Let's head out at first light, then.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.650
Hey.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.720
I made these for everyone.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:47.860
Should shield you a bit, right?

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:52.870
I don't want anyone else to die.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.370
Yeah. Thank you.

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:00.630
Got you this, too, Kenroku.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.380
Oh! Thanks!

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:08.600
A guy I used to work with 
was skilled with these,

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.540
so I had him teach me how to use one.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:30.260
The battle's finally 
happening tomorrow, huh?

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.160
Back in my home town...

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:46.970
Back in my home town they say death 
will come soon if you see a red moon.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.640
Oh?

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:53.860
Looks bright to me.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.160
Guess that means I'm not dying anytime soon.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:05.340
I don't understand why, 
but the moon looks pretty red tonight.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.640
Hey, Shion, that's just 
some old folk nonsense.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.210
Maybe.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.110
Shion!

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:06.490
I saw the red moon,

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:13.400
so this is where my life ends.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.030
You idiot!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:23.400
I was the one who was supposed to die, 
if you hadn't protected me!

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:24.970
Please take...

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:30.980
Please take care of Okuni...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.310
Please.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:43.570
Okuni seems to have a fondness 
for you, as well, so...

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.840
Kenroku!

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.240
Ani-sama...

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:17.340
From now on, I'm your family.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.100
Mother.

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.460
Yukinojyo-san.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:38.940
The moon looks awfully red tonight.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.720
<b>"New Allies"</b>
